title: White Heat
text: One red laser and one doppler, and yet the ember in the grate must glow white. A fire has to be fed.
trick: a starburst fed by its own ray: one diagonal ray is bent (bender, mirror) round the doppler and back into the star square-on, so each pass adds the next colour until all its diagonal rays run white from a single red laser; a cyan filter then cuts the chimney beam out of that white
motif: a fire grate: a furnace in a wall of firebrick, occupied squares as bricks and open grid lines between them, an ember in the grate below, a chimney above with the cyan target
expect: merges>=1
---
L 0 12 2 r
*Z 9 12 0 k
*B 12 9 7 k
*R 12 12 1 k
*D 12 10 2 k
*B 6 9 4 k
*F 6 4 2 c
T 6 2 0 c
T 8 13 0 w
